  "prediction": "World A: parameter i is reported identifiable at (B, rho) iff P_ii > B^2 / rho^2, the reported count equals d_obs in the probe basis, every diagonal entry lies in its bracket, and off-diagonal entries are unrevealed. World B: when lambda_min rho^2 < B^2 < lambda_max rho^2 every eigenvalue, above and below the threshold, is recovered with error falling in the number of queries; outside that interval the oracle is constant and nothing is recovered. The first pilot (2026-09-09, pilot_v1.json) was designed on the wrong reading, that mixed probes reveal only above-threshold directions; it recovered below-threshold eigenvalues to 3 to 10 percent of chance at B from 1 to 2, and its max-margin estimator broke where the feasible set was wide; both corrected here before any seal.",
